From: A2Tools-patch <patch@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:35:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/31] Plugins: a widget the player resizes from its corners
 (a2.widget.resize)

A widget could only be resized by its plugin opening it again at a new
size; the Map overlay did that as its corner was dragged, a step every
50 ms, each one pinning the size and showing the window again, and lost
the drag when the button came up outside it: the player called it buggy.
await a2.widget.resize(edge), called on mousedown on a handle, now has the
window manager resize the widget from that edge or corner, as the meter's
own windows are: the size is unpinned (through the compositor on GNOME
and KDE), the host page starts the drag, and once the button is up the
size is pinned again and the widget hears it, a2.on("resized",
({ width, height }) => ...). Not while the widgets are locked, nor on
Windows, where a widget's window has no border to resize.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
